{number: 100}
{title: Sweet Hour of Prayer}
{key: D}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[D] Sweet hour of prayer, sweet [G] hour of prayer,
That [D] calls me from a [A7] world of care,
And [D] bids me at my [G] Father's throne,
Make [D] all my wants and [A7] wishes [D] known!
In [D] seasons of dis-[G] tress and grief,
My [D] soul has often [A7] found relief,
And [D] oft escaped the [G] tempter's snare,
By [D] thy return, sweet [A7] hour of [D] prayer.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[D] Sweet hour of prayer, sweet [G] hour of prayer,
The [D] joys I feel, the [A7] bliss I share
Of [D] those whose anxious [G] spirits burn
With [D] strong desires for [A7] thy re-[D] turn!
With [D] such I hasten [G] to the place
Where [D] God, my Saviour, [A7] shows His face,
And [D] gladly take my [G] station there,
And [D] wait for thee, sweet [A7] hour of [D] prayer.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[D] Sweet hour of prayer, sweet [G] hour of prayer,
Thy [D] wings shall my pe-[A7] tition bear
To [D] Him, whose truth and [G] faithfulness
En-[D] gage the waiting the [A7] soul to [D] bless:
And [D] since He bids me [G] seek His face,
Be-[D] lieve His Word, and [A7] trust His grace,
I'll [D] cast on Him my [G] ev'ry care,
And [D] wait for thee, sweet [A7] hour of [D] prayer.
{end_of_verse}
